IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-nouns`
IMPORT `rra-logic`
IMPORT `rra-part1-preliminary`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 July 2022 -- PART 4 REMEDIES (ss 8 to 8F).
--
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes / no (the words quoted at that branch),
-- NOTHING where it does not (tagged `NOTHING-kind (...)`).  What the Minister, the Commissioner or the Tribunal is
-- "satisfied" of, or considers "just and equitable", is for them and is an input; the amounts they fix are inputs.
-- Months are counted with `add months` (31 January plus one month is 28 or 29 February: fork F3).

§ `Part 4 -- Remedies`

§§ `Section 8 -- Remedies for unlawful dismissal on ground of age`

-- "Where any employee below the specified age": the employee's age at the dismissal, not at the representation (fork F12).
-- "within one month of the dismissal": the last day is the same day of the next month (fork F3).
-- src:602 | 8.—(1) Where any employee below the specified age considers that
-- src:603 | he or she has been unlawfully dismissed on the ground of age, he or
-- src:604 | she may, within one month of the dismissal, make representations in
-- src:605 | writing to the Minister to be reinstated in his or her former
-- src:606 | employment.
@ref s 8(1) (src:602-606)
GIVEN `the date of the dismissal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8(1) the last day on which the employee can make representations to the Minister` MEANS
    `add months` `the date of the dismissal` 1

@ref s 8(1) (src:602-606)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the date of the dismissal` IS A DATE
      `the employee considers that he or she has been unlawfully dismissed on the ground of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the representations are made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) the employee may make representations in writing to the Minister to be reinstated` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (employment's `date of birth`) (`s 2(1) "specified age" the employee's specified age` employment)
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the date on which the employee attains the specified age cannot be worked out (29 February birth, no anniversary date)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST attained THEN
        IF `the date of the dismissal` LESS THAN attained AND `the employee considers that he or she has been unlawfully dismissed on the ground of age`
        THEN
            IF `the date the representations are made` AT MOST `s 8(1) the last day on which the employee can make representations to the Minister` `the date of the dismissal`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "within one month of the dismissal"; the representations are made after that, and the subsection does not say that they may not be
                NOTHING
        ELSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for "any employee below the specified age" who "considers that he or she has been unlawfully dismissed on the ground of age"; the case falls outside
            NOTHING

-- src:608 | (2) The Minister may, before making a decision on any such
-- src:609 | representations, direct the Commissioner in writing to inquire and
-- src:610 | report whether in the Commissioner’s opinion the employee has been
-- src:611 | unlawfully dismissed on the ground of age.
@ref s 8(2) (src:608-611)
GIVEN `representations have been made to the Minister under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has not yet made a decision on them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2) the Minister may direct the Commissioner in writing to inquire and report` MEANS
    IF `representations have been made to the Minister under subsection (1)` AND `the Minister has not yet made a decision on them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "before making a decision on any such representations"; there are none, or the decision has been made
        NOTHING

-- "If, after considering any report made by the Commissioner under subsection (2)": where no report was made there is
-- none to consider, and the input is true.
-- src:613 | (3) If, after considering any report made by the Commissioner
-- src:614 | under subsection (2), the Minister is satisfied that the employee has
-- src:615 | been unlawfully dismissed by his or her employer on the ground of
-- src:616 | age, the Minister may, despite any rule of law or agreement to the
-- src:617 | contrary —
-- src:619 | (a) direct the employer to reinstate the employee in the
-- src:620 | employee’s former employment and to pay the employee
-- src:621 | an amount that is equivalent to the salary that the employee
-- src:622 | would have earned had he or she not been unlawfully
-- src:623 | dismissed by the employer; or
-- src:625 | (b) direct the employer to pay such amount of salary as
-- src:626 | compensation as the Minister may consider just and
-- src:627 | equitable having regard to all the circumstances of the
-- src:628 | case,
@ref s 8(3) (src:613-628)
GIVEN `any report made by the Commissioner under subsection (2) has been considered by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the employee has been unlawfully dismissed by his or her employer on the ground of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) the Minister may direct the employer to reinstate and pay, or to pay compensation` MEANS
    IF `any report made by the Commissioner under subsection (2) has been considered by the Minister` AND `the Minister is satisfied that the employee has been unlawfully dismissed by his or her employer on the ground of age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for the Minister who, "after considering any report made by the Commissioner under subsection (2)", "is satisfied that the employee has been unlawfully dismissed by his or her employer on the ground of age"; the case falls outside
        NOTHING

-- src:630 | and the employer must comply with the direction of the Minister.
@ref s 8(3) closing (src:630)
GIVEN `the Minister gave a direction to the employer under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer complied with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) the employer has complied with the direction of the Minister` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Minister gave a direction to the employer under subsection (3)`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to comply with "the direction of the Minister" under subsection (3); none was given
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the employer complied with the direction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the employer must comply with the direction of the Minister" -- a requirement not met (marginal reading (a))
            JUST FALSE

@ref s 8(3) closing (src:630)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`s 8(3) the employer must comply with the direction of the Minister` MEANS
    PARTY Employer
    MUST `comply with the direction of the Minister`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Employer BECAUSE "s 8(3): the employer did not comply with the direction of the Minister"

-- "must, in particular, have regard to": the five are the Act's own, and the list is not closed.
-- src:632 | (4) In determining the amount of compensation to be awarded
-- src:633 | under subsection (3), the Minister must, in particular, have regard
-- src:634 | to —
-- src:641 | (a) the loss sustained by the employee in consequence of the
-- src:642 | unlawful dismissal;
-- src:644 | (b) the employee’s prospects in obtaining alternative
-- src:645 | employment;
-- src:647 | (c) the steps taken by the employee to mitigate his or her loss;
-- src:649 | (d) the period the employee has served with the employer; and
-- src:650 | (e) the employee’s age.
@ref s 8(4) (src:632-650)
GIVEN consideration IS A `Consideration in fixing compensation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(4) the Minister must have regard to the consideration` MEANS
    CONSIDER consideration
    WHEN `the loss sustained by the employee in consequence of the unlawful dismissal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the employee's prospects in obtaining alternative employment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the steps taken by the employee to mitigate his or her loss` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the period the employee has served with the employer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the employee's age` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the Minister must "in particular" have regard to (a) to (e); the subsection does not say whether regard must, or may not, be had to anything else
    WHEN `the tripartite guidelines` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the steps taken by the employer to re-employ the employee` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `any other consideration` THEN NOTHING

-- Finality: the text says the decision is final; whether a court may still review it is not said.
-- src:652 | (5) The decision of the Minister on any representation made under
-- src:653 | this section is final.
@ref s 8(5) (src:652-653)
GIVEN `the decision is the Minister's decision on a representation made under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(5) the decision of the Minister on the representation is final` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the Minister's decision on a representation made under section 8`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): finality is of "The decision of the Minister on any representation made under this section"
        NOTHING

-- src:655 | (6) Any direction of the Minister under subsection (3) operates as a
-- src:656 | bar to any action for damages by the employee in any court in respect
-- src:657 | of the unlawful dismissal on the ground of age.
@ref s 8(6) (src:655-657)
GIVEN `the Minister gave a direction under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(6) the employee may bring an action for damages in a court in respect of the unlawful dismissal` MEANS
    IF `the Minister gave a direction under subsection (3)`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any direction of the Minister under subsection (3) operates as a bar to any action for damages by the employee in any court in respect of the unlawful dismissal on the ground of age"
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is of "Any direction of the Minister under subsection (3)"; there is none
        NOTHING

-- src:659 | (7) An employer who fails to comply with the direction of the
-- src:660 | Minister under subsection (3) shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:661 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:662 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 8(7) (src:659-662)
GIVEN `the employer failed to comply with the direction of the Minister under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(7) the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer failed to comply with the direction of the Minister under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of "An employer who fails to comply with the direction of the Minister under subsection (3)"
        NOTHING

@ref s 8(7) (src:659-662)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 8(7) the penalty on conviction` MEANS Penalty OF 10_000, 12

@ref s 8(7) (src:659-662)
GIVEN `the employer has been convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(7) the sentence is within the penalty` MEANS
    IF NOT `the employer has been convicted`
    THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is one the employer is "liable on conviction" to; there has been no conviction
        NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the fine and the term are within the ceilings` (`s 8(7) the penalty on conviction`) `the fine in dollars` `the imprisonment in months`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both"
            JUST FALSE

-- The amount to be paid is the Minister's to fix and is an input; what remains unpaid is the amount less what was paid.
-- src:664 | (8) Where any amount to be paid by an employer under
-- src:665 | subsection (3) is not paid in accordance with the direction of the
-- src:666 | Minister and the employer has been convicted of an offence under
-- src:667 | subsection (7), the amount or so much thereof as remains unpaid is
-- src:668 | recoverable by the court as if it were a fine and the amount so
-- src:669 | recovered is to be paid to the employee entitled to payment under the
-- src:670 | direction of the Minister.
@ref s 8(8) (src:664-670)
GIVEN `the amount payable under the direction` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the employer has been convicted of an offence under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 8(8) the amount recoverable by the court as if it were a fine` MEANS
    IF `the employer has been convicted of an offence under subsection (7)` AND `the amount paid` LESS THAN `the amount payable under the direction`
    THEN JUST (`the amount payable under the direction` MINUS `the amount paid`)
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amount is recoverable "where any amount ... is not paid in accordance with the direction of the Minister and the employer has been convicted of an offence under subsection (7)"; the case falls outside
        NOTHING

-- src:672 | (9) The Minister may, by writing under the hand of the Minister,
-- src:673 | delegate all or any of the Minister’s powers under this section (except
-- src:674 | this power of delegation) to any public officer.
@ref s 8(9) (src:672-674)
GIVEN `the power is a power under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is the power of delegation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegate is a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegation is by writing under the hand of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(9) the Minister may delegate the power` MEANS
    IF `the power is the power of delegation`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "delegate all or any of the Minister's powers under this section (except this power of delegation)"
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the power is a power under section 8` AND `the delegate is a public officer` AND `the delegation is by writing under the hand of the Minister`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "the Minister's powers under this section" "by writing under the hand of the Minister" "to any public officer"; the case falls outside
            NOTHING

-- src:676 | (10) A delegation under subsection (9) is revocable at will and no
-- src:677 | delegation prevents the exercise of any power by the Minister.
@ref s 8(10) (src:676-677)
GIVEN `a delegation was made under subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(10) the delegation is revocable at will` MEANS
    IF `a delegation was made under subsection (9)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is of "A delegation under subsection (9)"
        NOTHING

@ref s 8(10) (src:676-677)
GIVEN `a delegation was made under subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(10) the delegation prevents the Minister from exercising the power` MEANS
    IF `a delegation was made under subsection (9)`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no delegation prevents the exercise of any power by the Minister"
        JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is of "A delegation under subsection (9)"; there is none
        NOTHING

-- src:679 | (11) A power so delegated, when exercised by the delegate, is for
-- src:680 | the purposes of this section deemed to have been exercised by the
-- src:681 | Minister.
@ref s 8(11) (src:679-681)
GIVEN `the power was delegated under subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegate exercised the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(11) the power exercised by the delegate is deemed to have been exercised by the Minister` MEANS
    IF `the power was delegated under subsection (9)` AND `the delegate exercised the power`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is of "A power so delegated, when exercised by the delegate"
        NOTHING

§§ `Section 8A -- Conciliation, etc.`

-- Two paragraphs of section 8A(4) are the matters that route an employee through section 8A(1) and the other two
-- through section 8A(3).  These two helpers are not rules of the Act.
GIVEN matter IS A `Dispute matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`matter referred to in section 8A(4)(a) or (b)` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `denial of re-employment because the employee does not satisfy the eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `denial of re-employment, in accordance with section 7C(1), because the employer is unable to find a suitable vacancy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the reasonableness of the terms and conditions of a re-employment offer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the reasonableness of the amount of an employment assistance payment offered` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another matter` THEN FALSE

GIVEN matter IS A `Dispute matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`matter referred to in section 8A(4)(c) or (d)` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `denial of re-employment because the employee does not satisfy the eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `denial of re-employment, in accordance with section 7C(1), because the employer is unable to find a suitable vacancy` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the reasonableness of the terms and conditions of a re-employment offer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the reasonableness of the amount of an employment assistance payment offered` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another matter` THEN FALSE

-- "a re-employment dispute means a dispute over any of the following matters": a closed list.
-- src:719 | (4) For the purposes of this Part, a re-employment dispute means a
-- src:720 | dispute over any of the following matters:
-- src:722 | (a) the denial of re-employment to an employee on the ground
-- src:723 | that the employee does not satisfy the eligibility criteria set
-- src:724 | out in section 7(1);
-- src:726 | (b) the denial of re-employment, in accordance with
-- src:727 | section 7C(1), to an employee on the ground that the
-- src:728 | employer is unable to find a vacancy in the employer’s
-- src:729 | establishment which is suitable for the employee;
-- src:736 | (c) the reasonableness of the terms and conditions of any
-- src:737 | re-employment offer made pursuant to section 7A(1) or
-- src:738 | (3)(a)(i) by an employer;
-- src:740 | (d) the reasonableness of the amount of any employment
-- src:741 | assistance payment offered to an employee pursuant to
-- src:742 | section 7C(1)(a).
@ref s 8A(4) (src:719-742)
GIVEN matter IS A `Dispute matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(4) the dispute is a re-employment dispute` MEANS
    IF `matter referred to in section 8A(4)(a) or (b)` matter OR `matter referred to in section 8A(4)(c) or (d)` matter
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a re-employment dispute means a dispute over any of the following matters"
        JUST FALSE

-- (1): the last day is the same day of the next month after the last day of employment (fork F3).
-- src:690 | 8A.—(1) An employee who has a re-employment dispute with his
-- src:691 | or her employer which relates to any matter referred to in
-- src:692 | subsection (4)(a) or (b) must, before making any representation to
-- src:693 | the Minister under section 8B, first notify the Commissioner in
-- src:694 | writing of the re-employment dispute no later than one month after
-- src:695 | the last day of the employee’s employment with his or her employer.
@ref s 8A(1) (src:690-695)
GIVEN matter IS A `Dispute matter`
      `the last day of the employee's employment with his or her employer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 8A(1) the last day on which the employee can notify the Commissioner of the re-employment dispute` MEANS
    IF `matter referred to in section 8A(4)(a) or (b)` matter
    THEN JUST (`add months` `the last day of the employee's employment with his or her employer` 1)
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of an employee with a re-employment dispute "which relates to any matter referred to in subsection (4)(a) or (b)"
        NOTHING

@ref s 8A(1) (src:690-695)
GIVEN matter IS A `Dispute matter`
      `the last day of the employee's employment with his or her employer` IS A DATE
      `the date the employee notified the Commissioner in writing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(1) the employee notified the Commissioner in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 8A(1) the last day on which the employee can notify the Commissioner of the re-employment dispute` matter `the last day of the employee's employment with his or her employer`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of an employee with a re-employment dispute "which relates to any matter referred to in subsection (4)(a) or (b)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST deadline THEN
        IF `the date the employee notified the Commissioner in writing` AT MOST deadline
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... first notify the Commissioner in writing of the re-employment dispute no later than one month after the last day of the employee's employment with his or her employer" -- marginal reading (a)
            JUST FALSE

-- The clock starts on the last day of employment (day 0).
@ref s 8A(1) (src:690-695)
GIVEN `the last day of the employee's employment with his or her employer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`s 8A(1) the employee must notify the Commissioner in writing of the re-employment dispute` MEANS
    PARTY Employee
    MUST `notify the Commissioner in writing of the re-employment dispute`
    WITHIN (Day (`add months` `the last day of the employee's employment with his or her employer` 1) MINUS Day `the last day of the employee's employment with his or her employer`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Employee BECAUSE "s 8A(1): the Commissioner was not notified in writing of the re-employment dispute within one month after the last day of employment"

-- (2): an employee who attains the specified age on or after 1 January 2012 and considers that he or she was dismissed
-- without just cause or excuse on or after the date of attaining it.
-- src:699 | (2) An employee (being an employee who attains the specified age
-- src:700 | on or after 1 January 2012) who considers that he or she has been
-- src:701 | dismissed without just cause or excuse by his or her employer on or
-- src:702 | after the date the employee attains the specified age must, before
-- src:703 | making any representation to the Minister under section 8B, first
-- src:704 | notify the Commissioner in writing of the dismissal no later than
-- src:705 | one month after the last day of the employee’s employment with the
-- src:706 | employer.
@ref s 8A(2) (src:699-706)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the employee considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or excuse on or after the date the employee attains the specified age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 8A(2) the last day on which the employee can notify the Commissioner of the dismissal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (employment's `date of birth`) (`s 2(1) "specified age" the employee's specified age` employment)
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the date on which the employee attains the specified age cannot be worked out (29 February birth, no anniversary date)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST attained THEN
        IF attained AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2012) AND `the employee considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or excuse on or after the date the employee attains the specified age`
        THEN JUST (`add months` `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer` 1)
        ELSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "An employee (being an employee who attains the specified age on or after 1 January 2012) who considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or excuse by his or her employer on or after the date the employee attains the specified age"
            NOTHING

@ref s 8A(2) (src:699-706)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the employee considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or excuse on or after the date the employee attains the specified age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer` IS A DATE
      `the date the employee notified the Commissioner in writing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(2) the employee notified the Commissioner in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 8A(2) the last day on which the employee can notify the Commissioner of the dismissal` employment `the employee considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or excuse on or after the date the employee attains the specified age` `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST deadline THEN
        IF `the date the employee notified the Commissioner in writing` AT MOST deadline
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... first notify the Commissioner in writing of the dismissal no later than one month after the last day of the employee's employment with the employer" -- marginal reading (a)
            JUST FALSE

@ref s 8A(2) (src:699-706)
GIVEN `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`s 8A(2) the employee must notify the Commissioner in writing of the dismissal` MEANS
    PARTY Employee
    MUST `notify the Commissioner in writing of the dismissal`
    WITHIN (Day (`add months` `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer` 1) MINUS Day `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Employee BECAUSE "s 8A(2): the Commissioner was not notified in writing of the dismissal within one month after the last day of employment"

-- (3): six months, counted with `add months` (fork F3).
-- src:708 | (3) An employee who has a re-employment dispute with his or her
-- src:709 | employer which relates to any matter referred to in subsection (4)(c)
-- src:710 | or (d) must, before lodging a claim against the employer under
-- src:711 | section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016, submit to the
-- src:712 | Commissioner, under section 3(1) of that Act, not later than 6 months
-- src:713 | after the last day of the employee’s employment with the employer, a
-- src:714 | mediation request for the mediation under Part 2 of that Act of the
-- src:715 | re-employment dispute.
@ref s 8A(3) (src:708-715)
GIVEN matter IS A `Dispute matter`
      `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 8A(3) the last day on which the employee can submit a mediation request` MEANS
    IF `matter referred to in section 8A(4)(c) or (d)` matter
    THEN JUST (`add months` `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer` 6)
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of an employee with a re-employment dispute "which relates to any matter referred to in subsection (4)(c) or (d)"
        NOTHING

@ref s 8A(3) (src:708-715)
GIVEN matter IS A `Dispute matter`
      `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer` IS A DATE
      `the date the employee submitted the mediation request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(3) the employee submitted the mediation request in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 8A(3) the last day on which the employee can submit a mediation request` matter `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST deadline THEN
        IF `the date the employee submitted the mediation request` AT MOST deadline
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... submit to the Commissioner ... not later than 6 months after the last day of the employee's employment with the employer, a mediation request" -- marginal reading (a)
            JUST FALSE

@ref s 8A(3) (src:708-715)
GIVEN `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`s 8A(3) the employee must submit a mediation request to the Commissioner` MEANS
    PARTY Employee
    MUST `submit a mediation request to the Commissioner`
    WITHIN (Day (`add months` `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer` 6) MINUS Day `the last day of the employee's employment with the employer`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Employee BECAUSE "s 8A(3): a mediation request was not submitted to the Commissioner within 6 months after the last day of employment"

