§§ `Section 8C -- Remedies relating to unreasonable terms and conditions and employment assistance payment`

-- src:913 | 8C.—(1) An employee who has a re-employment dispute with his
-- src:914 | or her employer which relates to any matter referred to in
-- src:915 | section 8A(4)(c) or (d) may, if a claim referral certificate is issued
-- src:916 | in respect of that dispute, lodge a claim for employment assistance
-- src:917 | payment with an Employment Claims Tribunal under section 13 of
-- src:918 | the Employment Claims Act 2016.
@ref s 8C(1) (src:913-918)
GIVEN matter IS A `Dispute matter`
      `a claim referral certificate is issued in respect of that dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8C(1) the employee may lodge a claim for employment assistance payment with an Employment Claims Tribunal` MEANS
    IF `matter referred to in section 8A(4)(c) or (d)` matter AND `a claim referral certificate is issued in respect of that dispute`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `matter referred to in section 8A(4)(c) or (d)` matter
         THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the employee "may, if a claim referral certificate is issued in respect of that dispute, lodge a claim"; no certificate is issued, so the "if" is not met and the permission does not arise (fork F21, marginal reading (a))
            JUST FALSE
         ELSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for an employee with a re-employment dispute "which relates to any matter referred to in section 8A(4)(c) or (d)"; the matter is not one of those, and the clause that narrows the grant has no "if", "only" or "unless" (fork F21)
            NOTHING

